## Bug diagnosis (confirmed experimentally, in a throwaway copy under /tmp, now deleted)
`FileAttachment` interpolates the filename into the quoted `filename="..."` parameter **without escaping `"` or `\`**. For an ASCII filename containing a double quote (or backslash) the header is malformed / injectable:
- `new_filename.go` → `attachment; filename="new_filename.go"` (correct)
- `new"filename.go` → `attachment; filename="new"filename.go"` (WRONG; quote not escaped)
- `new\filename.go` → `attachment; filename="new\filename.go"` (WRONG; backslash not escaped)
- `new🧡_filename.go` → `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''new%F0%9F%A7%A1_filename.go` (correct, UTF-8 branch already uses `url.QueryEscape`)

